      },
      "message": "fix(turning): Facing, Profile Rough and Profile Finish take a start and an exit pick\n\nA turning pick is a point in the lathe (Z, X) plane: a model point with\na Z, read as (station, radius) about the fitted axis. The first pass\nstarts at the start pick and the last pass leaves at the exit pick.\n\n- motion: `turning::with_picks` lays the picks on the finished path of a\n  kernel. No pick returns the path unchanged. A pick that is not in air,\n  is on the chuck side, or whose move crosses the stock or the part is\n  refused by name and never moved.\n- app: the registry has `PickCapability::Meridian` for the three kinds.\n  A pick without a Z is refused at the command door. Threading says that\n  the thread start law sets its start.\n- mcp: `edit_operation` and `list_operation_types` name the lathe plane.\n- ui: typed Start point / Exit point groups on the Geometry tab.\n\nSlice 1 of #3331. The eight other turning kinds keep the \"owed\" row.\n\nRefs #3331\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
